# File: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute-supervisor.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/395-classify-failed-consumed-dispatch-worker-after-post-resume-cleanup/requirements.md

Feature: Classify failed consumed-dispatch worker after post-resume cleanup
  A resumed consumed invocation must stop owning recovery classification after its
  fresh failed worker and proven-owned pane are fully settled.

  @AC1 @AC6 @SCN001
  Scenario: Fresh resumed implementation failure settles ephemeral dispatch state
    Given a consumed repaired-publication dispatch starts the standard implement worker
    And the fresh worker returns a strict failed implementation intervention handoff
    When the proven-owned terminal worker pane closes and the worker entry is removed
    Then consumedDispatch is removed in the persisted transition
    And the fresh ordinary failure and handoff remain available for classification

  @AC2 @SCN002
  Scenario: Settlement preserves one-time recovery authority
    Given the consumed dispatch binds one original recovery tuple, safe-recovery record, and archived source handoff
    When the fresh resumed worker failure settles
    Then the tuple, record, archive identity, digest, source evidence, and stopped disposition remain unchanged
    And no invocation is replayed and no recovery or allowance is appended or minted

  @AC3 @AC6 @SCN003
  Scenario: Parameter-free discovery uses the ordinary amended-spec path
    Given fresh failure settlement removed the stale ephemeral dispatch marker
    And a singular Approved specification amendment now satisfies ordinary intervention proof
    When parameter-free recovery discovery runs
    Then discovery classifies the fresh failure through the ordinary approved intervention path
    And it does not offer the old consumed invocation or require a run checkpoint edit

  @AC4 @SCN004
  Scenario Outline: Unsettled consumed dispatch remains fail-closed
    Given an otherwise matching resumed consumed dispatch with <defect>
    When the failure path and parameter-free discovery run
    Then consumedDispatch remains authoritative and blocked
    And no recovery authority or evidence is changed

    Examples:
      | defect |
      | missing handoff |
      | malformed handoff |
      | archived source handoff replayed as fresh |
      | wrong issue step worker or pane identity |
      | active worker |
      | live pane after incomplete cleanup |
      | pane close failure |

  @AC5 @SCN005
  Scenario: Existing consumed-dispatch states keep their behavior
    Given prepared, pending, stopped-resumable, started-live, repeated, and successful fixtures from issue 394
    When their supervisor and discovery paths run
    Then one-time same-invocation behavior remains unchanged
    And only proven fresh failed-intervention settlement enters ordinary classification
